From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: drop the cmake<4 pin so a riscv64 wheel resolves

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [cmake's own PyPI riscv64 wheel only exists from 4.0 on]

The `cmake` PyPI project has never published a riscv64 wheel for any
3.x release -- checked its full release history via PyPI JSON, zero
riscv64 files anywhere below 4.0 -- so `pip install "cmake<4"` (both
this workflow's own CIBW_BEFORE_BUILD step and the identical pin in
[build-system].requires, which build isolation installs the same way)
can never resolve a prebuilt wheel on riscv64 and instead builds
CMake's own C++ source tree from scratch, which fails here with
"Could NOT find OpenSSL" out of CMake's bundled curl
(Utilities/cmcurl/CMakeLists.txt) -- a build dependency this image
carries nowhere near the rest of this package's own dependency list.

CMakeLists.txt's own cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.16) is well
clear of CMake 4.0's removed-compatibility floor (3.5), and nothing
else in this tree pins a sub-4.0 CMake feature, so dropping the upper
bound lets pip resolve cmake's real riscv64 wheel
(cmake-4.4.4-py3-none-manylinux_2_31_riscv64.whl) instead of building
from source at all.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 89aee80..3cc7d79 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 [build-system]
 requires = [
-  "cmake<4",
+  "cmake",
   "conan>=2",
   "ninja",
   "scikit-build",
